  "sourceUse": "The dated programme page (39838) and detailed full-time table both allocate 12 EC of open choice in year two and 30 EC in year three. The public prose says 48 EC of choice without reconciling it with its own detailed table; the dated credit groups control the allocation. This route records 42 EC genuinely open and 24 EC restricted across both years. The programme table groups zero-credit tutoring in every year and a required writing diagnostic in year one separately from the 180 EC.",
  "progression": {
    "yearOne": "Nine credit-bearing modules total 60 EC. Nederlands als wetenschap 1 covers linguistics and language use; the parallel second course introduces historical and modern Dutch literature. The 6 EC first-year research component is Kruispunten. The Faculty OER part A Articles A6.4 and A6.6 set the ordinary full-time positive binding study advice threshold at 48 EC from the first year.",
    "yearTwo": "Stilistiek (block 1) and Dynamiek van het Nederlands: theorie (block 2) precede both 3 EC methods workshops (block 3). Dynamiek requires introductory linguistics, supplied by Nederlands als wetenschap 1. Taallab lists Stilistiek, Dynamiek and at least one methods workshop or equivalent background. Taallab runs in block 4. Literature, Landscape and Ecology runs in block 5 alongside the start of the 12 EC writing workshop, whose formal course entry requires the completed first year and whose listed subject preparation includes the research courses. Full-time study takes both methods workshops and both 6 EC courses.",
    "yearThree": "The public table lists linguistics first among four coherent 12 EC pairs. Taal en theorie requires all first-year courses and Dynamiek; Specialization Linguistics requires positive binding study advice or dispensation. Both are scheduled in block 4. The two project entries require positive binding study advice, completed first year, at least 24 EC of year-two prescribed and coherent choice coursework and attendance of a qualifying 12 EC year-three pair. The detailed list also specifies philosophy, two restricted choices, both methods workshops and at least one of Taallab and Literature, Landscape and Ecology. The selected route completes all of them and Tekstwerk before the concurrent block-5 writing workshop and blocks-5–6 research project.",
    "openChoice": "Retain both dated open-choice allocations without naming a placement, minor or specific elective. The public page describes an optional placement of up to 12 EC and gives other examples for using elective space."
  }
